Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.32,0:00:22.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[tense music plays]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.99,0:00:26.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[woman wailing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.33,0:00:30.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[midwife] Breathe, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.12,0:00:32.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[wailing continues]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.04,0:00:35.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Push!{\i0}\N{\i1}-[doctor] Breathe!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.58,0:00:36.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[midwife] Yes! Yes!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.25,0:00:39.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Grace, I shall need you to push.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.63,0:00:42.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Duchess of Hastings wailing]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[midwife] Very good. Yes!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.51,0:00:45.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You must breathe, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.30,0:00:47.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Someone must tell me something!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.39,0:00:50.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Would you move?{\i0}\N{\i1}-What are you doing in here, Lady Danbury?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.06,0:00:53.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I am going in, Your Grace.{\i0}\N{\i1}-No place for a lady in there.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.98,0:00:56.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Someone must be with her.{\i0}\N{\i1}If not her husband, then--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.64,0:00:58.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Duchess of Hastings screams]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.15,0:01:04.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[wailing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.78,0:01:06.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[groans loudly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.40,0:01:07.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[doctor] Push.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.74,0:01:09.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I must know{\i0}\N{\i1}if I am at long last to have a son.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.78,0:01:11.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[doctor] Forceps.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.20,0:01:12.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[wailing continues]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.83,0:01:16.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I can see the head. Push!{\i0}\N{\i1}-Push!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.75,0:01:18.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Tell me!{\i0}\N{\i1}-Tell him!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.42,0:01:19.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Breathe, Your Grace!{\i0}\N{\i1}-Yes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.54,0:01:21.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Push.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Push, Your Grace! Push!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.46,0:01:24.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What is it? What is it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.71,0:01:25.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[baby gurgles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.59,0:01:27.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is a boy, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.97,0:01:30.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[baby crying]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.29,0:01:58.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[baby coos]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.67,0:02:00.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have a son.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.00,0:02:02.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have a son!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.55,0:02:05.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[all cheering]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.76,0:02:07.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sarah!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.22,0:02:12.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I finally gave him…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.06,0:02:14.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}a son.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.06,0:02:18.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.43,0:02:19.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[exhales]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.15,0:02:21.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasps]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.60,0:02:23.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[struggling breaths]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.48,0:02:25.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sarah.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.40,0:02:26.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Doctor!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.57,0:02:29.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There is too much blood.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.53,0:02:31.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sarah…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.66,0:02:36.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Duke of Hastings] A perfect son!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.29,0:02:41.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Simon Arthur Henry Fitzranulph Basset,{\i0}\N{\i1}the next Duke of Hastings!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.37,0:02:42.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[all cheering]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.05,0:02:53.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[maid] Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.14,0:02:56.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Would you like us to arrange{\i0}\N{\i1}the duchess's room for you?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.47,0:02:59.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.02,0:03:01.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That will not be necessary.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.62,0:03:18.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">There will forever be just two words{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.29,0:03:20.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that come to this author's mind{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.25,0:03:22.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the morning after any good party,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.50,0:03:25.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8}{\i1}"shock" and "delight."{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.67,0:03:31.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8}{\i1}Well, dear reader, the scandalous accounts{\i0}\N{\i1}from last night's soiree at Vauxhall{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.63,0:03:35.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8}{\i1}are quite shocking and delightful indeed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.43,0:03:37.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It has arrived, Your Majesty!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.56,0:03:41.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}At once! At once!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.52,0:03:45.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Emerging, phoenix-like{\i0}\N{\i1}from the ashes of irrelevance{\i0}<span style="style1">,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.90,0:03:49.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}is one Miss Daphne Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.69,0:03:55.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The illustrious debutante{\i0}\N{\i1}was seen dancing not once, but twice{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.20,0:03:59.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}with the season's most eligible{\i0}\N{\i1}and most uncatchable rake,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.33,0:04:01.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the Duke of Hastings.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.41,0:04:03.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Where are you going so early, Your Grace?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.83,0:04:06.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}To promenade.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.22,0:04:20.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Lady Danbury] He is smiling.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Violet giggles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.47,0:04:22.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Danbury] The duke rarely smiles.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.14,0:04:24.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne has an excellent sense of humor.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.27,0:04:25.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She will need it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.73,0:04:28.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Life as a duchess will have many demands.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.56,0:04:29.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hosting balls,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.82,0:04:31.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}greeting foreign dignitaries…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.57,0:04:33.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne will not merely be {\i0}<span style="style2">in {\i0}{\i1}society.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.78,0:04:35.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She will be leading it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.20,0:04:37.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have prepared her quite well,{\i0}\N{\i1}Lady Danbury.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.20,0:04:38.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.20,0:04:39.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both laugh]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.62,0:04:41.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Eight balls.{\i0}\N{\i1}-No.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.37,0:04:44.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Eight balls.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.16,0:04:47.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You do want our plan to succeed,{\i0}\N{\i1}do you not?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.58,0:04:48.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The purpose of this arrangement{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.96,0:04:51.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}is to keep the marriage-minded mothers{\i0}\N{\i1}of the ton at bay,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.21,0:04:53.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}not hurl myself{\i0}\N{\i1}directly into the lion's den.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.38,0:04:57.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The purpose of this arrangement is{\i0}\N{\i1}to ensure I marry my very first season.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.18,0:04:59.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall grant you four.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.47,0:05:01.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Six balls.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Five.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.31,0:05:03.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Six. And you must send flowers.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.89,0:05:04.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Today.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.89,0:05:07.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Expensive ones.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Simon sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.73,0:05:10.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you were truly courting me,{\i0}\N{\i1}you'd buy out every florist in town.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.77,0:05:13.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If I were truly courting you,{\i0}\N{\i1}I would not need flowers,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.86,0:05:16.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}only five minutes alone{\i0}\N{\i1}with you in a drawing room.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.16,0:05:20.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I did not mean…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.66,0:05:22.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Six balls, Your Grace.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Very well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.66,0:05:24.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though I shall see about the flowers.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.45,0:05:26.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And you must remember,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.29,0:05:28.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}no one can know{\i0}\N{\i1}about our little arrangement.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.04,0:05:32.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Nor about what happened{\i0}\N{\i1}last night with Lord Berbrooke.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.59,0:05:34.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Ah, yes. How is your hand this morning?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.34,0:05:36.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You must know you did nothing wrong.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.01,0:05:40.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What I know is that even the rumor{\i0}\N{\i1}of my being alone with a man,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.93,0:05:43.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}let alone punching him, will ruin me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.02,0:05:47.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have no interest in causing a scandal, {\i0}\N{\i1}Miss Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.10,0:05:49.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I should imagine{\i0}\N{\i1}with you it comes naturally.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.69,0:05:51.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both chuckle softly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.32,0:05:53.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[horse neighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.36,0:05:57.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Penelope whispering] {\i0}\N{\i1}Of course I don't know. How would I know?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.74,0:06:01.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Because I can't ask her.{\i0}\N{\i1}Because I don't know how it happened.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.74,0:06:04.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's disturbing!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.16,0:06:05.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What are you girls talking about?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.87,0:06:09.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Penelope is wondering{\i0}\N{\i1}about Miss Thompson.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.58,0:06:10.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Prudence--{\i0}\N{\i1}-What of Miss Thompson?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.00,0:06:13.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Prudence] Penelope has inquiries.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Penelope] If you do not fall silent--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.05,0:06:15.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Philipa] About Miss Thompson's condition.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.80,0:06:17.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I beg your pardon?{\i0}\N{\i1}-They know, ma'am.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.80,0:06:20.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How did it happen, Mama?{\i0}\N{\i1}Is there to be a baby?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.68,0:06:22.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That will be enough.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.39,0:06:24.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My lord, are you hearing this?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.97,0:06:26.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What are we going to do?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.27,0:06:28.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There's no need for your hysterics.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.77,0:06:30.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why is Miss Thompson to be kept away?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.52,0:06:32.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Because her condition is catching.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.86,0:06:42.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So, Daphne may be in love.{\i0}\N{\i1}Does she think it an accomplishment?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.49,0:06:44.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What exactly has she accomplished, then?{\i0}\N{\i1}[scoffs] {\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.49,0:06:47.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She certainly did not build that man{\i0}\N{\i1}or bake him. He simply showed up.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.50,0:06:49.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Now he straggles about.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.54,0:06:52.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He likes her face, probably.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.08,0:06:53.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps her hair.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.33,0:06:55.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Having a nice face and pleasant hair{\i0}\N{\i1}is not an accomplishment.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.96,0:06:58.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you know what {\i0}<span style="style2">is {\i0}{\i1}an accomplishment? {\i0}\N{\i1}[laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.17,0:07:00.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Attending university!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.59,0:07:02.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If I were a man,{\i0}\N{\i1}I could do that, you know.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.76,0:07:05.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Instead, I shall have to stand by{\i0}\N{\i1}and watch dear Mama appear proud{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.64,0:07:08.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}because some man should like{\i0}\N{\i1}to admire my sister's face and hair{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.56,0:07:10.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and fill her up with babies!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.02,0:07:13.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, Penelope, you're not listening{\i0}\N{\i1}to a word I say.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.52,0:07:15.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Whoa! Oh!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.77,0:07:18.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know of someone… with child.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.61,0:07:20.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is it your mama?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.90,0:07:22.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is she not advanced in age?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.53,0:07:24.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I suppose your father{\i0}\N{\i1}should still want a boy--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.41,0:07:25.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is not Mama.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.95,0:07:27.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is a maid.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.99,0:07:30.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Which one of your maids is married?{\i0}\N{\i1}-She is not married.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.08,0:07:33.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How did she become with child{\i0}\N{\i1}if she is not married?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.17,0:07:35.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not know, but I will find out.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.17,0:07:37.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You must.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.21,0:07:39.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Otherwise, how can we make sure{\i0}\N{\i1}it never happens to us?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.59,0:07:41.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We have accomplishments to acquire.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.26,0:07:47.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Two dances? With a duke?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.51,0:07:49.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He was quite taken{\i0}\N{\i1}with your sister, Hyacinth.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.64,0:07:52.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The entire party was, for that matter.{\i0}\N{\i1}All eyes were on Daphne.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.98,0:07:55.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-At least enjoy some toast, dearest.{\i0}\N{\i1}-I am not hungry, Mama.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.86,0:07:58.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you certain the entire party{\i0}\N{\i1}was not simply eyeing a tear in her dress?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.86,0:08:00.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Or a misstep she took on the dance floor?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.69,0:08:03.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do wonder, Daphne, might we count{\i0}\N{\i1}on the duke at the Crawford ball?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.45,0:08:06.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I should think it a fair chance.{\i0}\N{\i1}-What about the Ramsbury ball, Friday?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.82,0:08:09.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-And what about the grand picnic?{\i0}\N{\i1}-We shall see, Mama.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.66,0:08:11.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Hyacinth] How terrible for Fran{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.20,0:08:13.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that she'll be off practicing pianoforte{\i0}\N{\i1}with Aunt Winnie all season{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.87,0:08:15.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and miss Daphne's engagement to the duke.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.79,0:08:17.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Gregory] {\i0}\N{\i1}Did Francesca leave for Bath?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.38,0:08:19.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How does a lady come to be with child?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.09,0:08:22.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Eloise, what a question!{\i0}\N{\i1}-I thought one needed to be married.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.88,0:08:25.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-What are you talking about?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Apparently, it's not even a requirement.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.80,0:08:26.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Eloise, that is enough.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.76,0:08:29.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, well…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.01,0:08:32.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne, you were playing so lovely.{\i0}\N{\i1}Please, do go on.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.98,0:08:37.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I take it the two of you know?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Do not look at me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.19,0:08:39.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Have you ever visited a farm, El?{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Eloise growls]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.73,0:08:42.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I hope you are not encouraging{\i0}\N{\i1}improper topics of conversation.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.40,0:08:43.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Benedict] Not at all, Mother.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.82,0:08:46.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}In fact, we were just heading off to…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.32,0:08:47.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}take our sticks out.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.32,0:08:49.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Colin Bridgerton!{\i0}\N{\i1}-A round of fencing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.08,0:08:54.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Miss? Humboldt is coming.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Humboldt is coming?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.58,0:08:56.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Humboldt?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Why is Humboldt coming?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.21,0:09:00.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Has someone arrived, Humboldt?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.59,0:09:03.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Callers for Miss Daphne, ma'am.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Daphne squeals, laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.30,0:09:06.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But… the duke.{\i0}\N{\i1}You already have a caller, dearest.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.09,0:09:08.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, I suppose now I have more.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.89,0:09:09.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.80,0:09:11.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[horses neighing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.23,0:09:21.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What is happening?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.66,0:09:28.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Coming through!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.50,0:09:36.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}When you said you will be taking me {\i0}\N{\i1}to your family…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.62,0:09:37.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Move!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.54,0:09:39.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}…I expected to be the only one present!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.75,0:09:41.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wore my satin knee breeches{\i0}\N{\i1}for the occasion!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.00,0:09:43.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Out of my way at once!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.26,0:09:50.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Dear God!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.43,0:09:52.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall speak to my soon-to-be--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.85,0:09:56.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-No, Lord Berbrooke, you must go.{\i0}\N{\i1}-You said you wanted this handled quickly.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.18,0:09:57.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You gave me your word.{\i0}\N{\i1}-I intend to keep it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.02,0:10:00.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You're the only man who proposed,{\i0}\N{\i1}therefore the only one I considered.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.77,0:10:03.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is nothing more{\i0}\N{\i1}than a terrible confusion.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.27,0:10:05.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For now, you must go,{\i0}\N{\i1}along with everyone else.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.24,0:10:11.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I should like to know what is going on.{\i0}\N{\i1}-I would like to know the very same.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.28,0:10:14.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps we might begin with why you chose{\i0}\N{\i1}to interrupt such an exquisite morning.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.79,0:10:16.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Because she is already engaged{\i0}\N{\i1}to be married.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.87,0:10:18.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The duke has already asked for your hand?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.66,0:10:20.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am not engaged, Mama.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.50,0:10:22.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Has anyone truly proposed to me? No.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.59,0:10:25.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Have I proposed to anyone else?{\i0}\N{\i1}I do not believe I have.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.55,0:10:28.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Do not be disrespectful, sister.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Disrespectful?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.80,0:10:31.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I cannot imagine{\i0}\N{\i1}a greater show of disrespect{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.59,0:10:33.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}than promising me to Nigel Berbrooke.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.72,0:10:35.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Anthony, tell me you did not.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.10,0:10:38.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-He's a fine choice. I looked into him.{\i0}\N{\i1}-You promised your sister to that man?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.43,0:10:40.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Not well enough, apparently.{\i0}\N{\i1}-What?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.40,0:10:42.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Does not matter.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.56,0:10:45.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I now have many choices indeed.{\i0}\N{\i1}I do not need--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.36,0:10:48.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have suitors.{\i0}\N{\i1}You do not have what matters: proposals.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.24,0:10:50.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Except, of course, from Lord Berbrooke.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.66,0:10:53.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Whatever happened to his eye?{\i0}\N{\i1}It's quite grotesque.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.53,0:10:57.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne has charmed a duke, Anthony.{\i0}\N{\i1}You must know that changes everything.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.20,0:10:59.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Please do not tell me{\i0}\N{\i1}this rebellion is to do with Hastings.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.66,0:11:00.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They are courting.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.62,0:11:02.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They've danced{\i0}\N{\i1}a couple of times together at a ball.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.88,0:11:04.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Colin has done the same with Penelope.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.79,0:11:05.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It does not signify--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.96,0:11:09.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They promenaded this morning,{\i0}\N{\i1}and he sent flowers today to both of us.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.51,0:11:11.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Expensive ones.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.10,0:11:17.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The duke is not a serious suitor.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.56,0:11:18.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He will never marry.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.81,0:11:20.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have known him since we were boys.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.60,0:11:24.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is not bravado,{\i0}\N{\i1}or denial, or even immaturity.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.48,0:11:25.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It appears that way to me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.82,0:11:28.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I will not marry Nigel Berbrooke.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.53,0:11:34.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have acted{\i0}\N{\i1}in your best interests, sister.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.49,0:11:37.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}One day, you will understand.{\i0}\N{\i1}One day, you will be most appreciative.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.74,0:11:39.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The contract to Berbrooke{\i0}\N{\i1}will be drawn up,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.87,0:11:41.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and you shall marry him.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.75,0:11:46.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[doors open, slam shut]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.54,0:11:49.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Mama…{\i0}\N{\i1}-You need not worry, dearest.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.17,0:11:51.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Once Lord Berbrooke witnesses{\i0}\N{\i1}the seriousness of the duke's intentions,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.97,0:11:53.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}he will have no choice but to retreat.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.43,0:11:56.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lord Berbrooke{\i0}\N{\i1}may not respect a woman's choice,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.43,0:11:58.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but he certainly will respect a man's.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.43,0:12:05.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, and if the duke is not… serious,{\i0}\N{\i1}I shall have others.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.73,0:12:09.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne, I saw the way the two of you{\i0}\N{\i1}looked at each other last night{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.11,0:12:10.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and this morning.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.03,0:12:12.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There are no others.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.49,0:12:14.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There is only the duke.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.07,0:12:17.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both chuckling]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.87,0:12:23.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[exhales]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[grunt echoing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.50,0:12:26.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon grunts]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.79,0:12:29.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did you truly dance{\i0}\N{\i1}with the Bridgerton girl? Twice?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.55,0:12:32.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[overlapping grunts]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.01,0:12:35.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Remind me again{\i0}\N{\i1}why you were the first person{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.09,0:12:38.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I chose to reacquaint myself with{\i0}\N{\i1}upon my return to town.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.14,0:12:39.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Admit it, friend.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Simon grunts]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.85,0:12:42.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You missed me.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Simon grunts, gasps]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.64,0:12:43.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[door opens]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.81,0:12:46.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon panting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.56,0:12:49.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Might I have a word?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Have as many as you like, Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.98,0:12:51.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[overlapping grunts and panting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.65,0:12:54.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You'll come down here,{\i0}\N{\i1}or must I come up there?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.49,0:13:00.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My fists have taken enough pounding{\i0}\N{\i1}from your chin today, Your Dukeship.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.28,0:13:01.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.25,0:13:05.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon sniffs, exhales]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.46,0:13:08.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Anthony grunts]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Simon grunts]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.21,0:13:09.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Anthony groans]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.59,0:13:11.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well? What seems to be so urgent?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.38,0:13:13.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'd like to know{\i0}\N{\i1}what was going through your head{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.38,0:13:14.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}last night and this morning.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.80,0:13:17.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have to be more precise. A great deal{\i0}\N{\i1}goes on in a mind as quick as mine.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.97,0:13:19.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you courting my sister?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.18,0:13:21.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Should I not be courting your sister?{\i0}\N{\i1}-No.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.14,0:13:24.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And I can think of dozens of reasons why,{\i0}\N{\i1}starting with, "She is my sister,"{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.31,0:13:26.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and ending with,{\i0}\N{\i1}"She is already engaged to be married,"{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.85,0:13:31.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and then perhaps circling back to,{\i0}\N{\i1}"She is my sister."{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.23,0:13:33.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Simon grunts]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Will laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.53,0:13:36.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was unaware of an engagement.{\i0}\N{\i1}Have the banns been read, then?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.65,0:13:38.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I assure you{\i0}\N{\i1}all the formal preparations are underway.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.86,0:13:40.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I arranged everything{\i0}\N{\i1}with Nigel Berbrooke,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.62,0:13:42.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}having given him my word.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.24,0:13:43.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So you have struck something squarely.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.83,0:13:46.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your problem is that Berbrooke{\i0}\N{\i1}is an unworthy suitor for Miss Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.96,0:13:49.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Simon grunts]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Anthony groans]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.08,0:13:50.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He is perfectly decent.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.50,0:13:53.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He is never seen going{\i0}\N{\i1}in and out of brothels, at least.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.00,0:13:56.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I even know where he's been{\i0}\N{\i1}the past few years, right here in London.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.72,0:13:59.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As opposed to some gambling hell,{\i0}\N{\i1}or backwater slum,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.39,0:14:02.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}or wherever it was you chose to fuck about{\i0}\N{\i1}for God knows whatever reason.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.01,0:14:05.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Anthony pants heavily]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.23,0:14:10.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Nigel Berbrooke is hardly a saint.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.73,0:14:12.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are and have long been a good friend.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.69,0:14:15.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The best, really. But this is my sister.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.23,0:14:18.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Think of all{\i0}\N{\i1}that we have shared as friends.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.53,0:14:21.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is furthest from my intentions{\i0}\N{\i1}to offend you,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.91,0:14:25.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but surely you can understand{\i0}\N{\i1}that family must come before all else!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.83,0:14:27.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[frustrated exhale]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.08,0:14:33.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Duke of Hastings]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">Why is he not saying anything?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.13,0:14:35.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He is four years old.{\i0}\N{\i1}He should be able to speak.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.46,0:14:39.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He is quite advanced in his letters,{\i0}\N{\i1}more so than any child I have taught.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.43,0:14:43.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He would have to be bloody Shakespeare{\i0}\N{\i1}with his letters if he cannot speak.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.60,0:14:44.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.51,0:14:46.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Let us hear it, boy.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.47,0:14:49.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Give me a word, a grunt.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.94,0:14:52.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Talk to me, damn you!{\i0}\N{\i1}-You're scaring him!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.56,0:14:55.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And if that is what it should take,{\i0}\N{\i1}I shall get a sound from him still.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.44,0:14:56.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.94,0:14:59.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What did you say?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.91,0:15:03.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}D-- D-- D-- D-- Do…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.28,0:15:06.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}n-- n-- n-- not…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.58,0:15:08.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What is he doing?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.25,0:15:12.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sharp rapid breathing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.46,0:15:15.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-He's an imbecile.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Your Grace--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.75,0:15:17.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He is an idiot!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.47,0:15:20.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My God.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.51,0:15:24.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you know how precarious{\i0}\N{\i1}of a situation we are in, boy?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.43,0:15:27.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We have been granted this line.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.56,0:15:30.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The monarchy itself has declared it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.68,0:15:32.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But it will only remain ours{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.44,0:15:35.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}so long as we remain extraordinary.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.11,0:15:39.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Hastings name cannot land{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.19,0:15:41.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}in the quivering hands of a half-wit!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.82,0:15:43.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Young Simon whimpers]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.53,0:15:46.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Get him out of my sight.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.03,0:15:48.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This boy is dead to me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.37,0:15:51.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[whimpering continues]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.92,0:15:55.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[horse neighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.09,0:16:02.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[knock at door]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.05,0:16:07.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I found you a few sweets.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.18,0:16:09.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I thought you might enjoy them{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.43,0:16:11.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}while everyone else{\i0}\N{\i1}attends tonight's ball.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.56,0:16:13.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You can come in.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.89,0:16:15.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm sure there's plenty to spare.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.82,0:16:28.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I hear they have decided{\i0}\N{\i1}not to send you home to your papa.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.74,0:16:33.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I dare say I am relieved.{\i0}\N{\i1}I can only imagine how he will react to…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.08,0:16:35.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your condition?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.58,0:16:38.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Marina…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.75,0:16:40.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}may I ask?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.67,0:16:42.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How did it happen?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.09,0:16:46.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Cake.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.22,0:16:49.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Cake?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.39,0:16:55.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Our vicar in Somerset{\i0}\N{\i1}was given to hours-long sermons.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.65,0:16:59.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Three, four,{\i0}\N{\i1}sometimes five hours they last.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.40,0:17:02.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would nearly swoon{\i0}\N{\i1}from hunger and fatigue.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.86,0:17:04.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Until one Sunday,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.57,0:17:07.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}just when I thought I'd have to crawl {\i0}\N{\i1}under the pew from exhaustion,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.78,0:17:09.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the eldest Crane boy, George…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.04,0:17:15.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sir George Crane sneaked me{\i0}\N{\i1}a wrapped bundle of cake and biscuits.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.04,0:17:17.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The vicar would've had his head{\i0}\N{\i1}if he knew.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.79,0:17:18.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Penelope chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.38,0:17:23.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}After some time,{\i0}\N{\i1}the bundles came to include small notes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.88,0:17:26.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We passed tiny missives{\i0}\N{\i1}back and forth for months.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.72,0:17:32.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've never longed for church {\i0}\N{\i1}quite so much.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.93,0:17:36.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-And where is Sir George now?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Spain.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.48,0:17:39.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He went off to fight with Wellington…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.81,0:17:41.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but he continued to write.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.65,0:17:43.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-See?{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Penelope gasps]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.20,0:17:48.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.66,0:17:52.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}your condition, then,{\i0}\N{\i1}it was brought about by…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.16,0:17:55.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Love.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.75,0:17:58.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It was love, Penelope.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.13,0:18:05.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[violin sonata playing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.93,0:18:09.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[dog barking]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.89,0:18:20.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Majesty, the royal physician{\i0}\N{\i1}has a report on the king.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.06,0:18:22.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How is it possible there's not been{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.65,0:18:24.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}a single compelling betrothal{\i0}\N{\i1}yet this season?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.65,0:18:27.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Terribly unexciting!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.24,0:18:30.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I could tell you a delicious tidbit{\i0}\N{\i1}about our former scullery maid.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.20,0:18:31.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I don't care about a dish wench.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.03,0:18:35.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wish to be entertained, enthralled.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.95,0:18:39.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Should the royal physician seek to tell me{\i0}\N{\i1}my husband is dead, Brimsley?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.96,0:18:41.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not believe so, Your Majesty.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.38,0:18:43.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then tell him I am occupied,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.17,0:18:44.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and bring me my stationery at once.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.70,0:19:13.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Rose] Will it be the rubies {\i0}\N{\i1}or the pearls, miss?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.70,0:19:14.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The pearls, of course.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.87,0:19:19.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mama, perhaps the rubies would better{\i0}\N{\i1}catch the eye of even more new suitors?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.92,0:19:24.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If I am not to put{\i0}\N{\i1}all my eggs in one basket,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.00,0:19:25.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I must…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.42,0:19:27.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}collect more…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.38,0:19:29.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-eggs.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Eloise, Violet laugh]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.80,0:19:31.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The duke truly has{\i0}\N{\i1}put your head in a spin.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.05,0:19:34.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}More like Lord Berbrooke{\i0}\N{\i1}must spin far away.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.05,0:19:36.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[doors open]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.14,0:19:39.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Good heavens. What is it, Mrs. Wilson?{\i0}\N{\i1}-The queen, ma'am.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.31,0:19:41.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Has she fallen ill?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Has King George caused her harm?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.73,0:19:46.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Her Majesty's royal stationery.{\i0}\N{\i1}-She has written to you, my lady.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.33,0:19:58.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-What does it say, Mama?{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Violet chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.92,0:20:07.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am invited to a private tea{\i0}\N{\i1}with the queen in two days' time.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.38,0:20:10.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Violet chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.05,0:20:14.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Never mind the pearls.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.30,0:20:17.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You shall wear{\i0}\N{\i1}the family diamonds tonight.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.97,0:20:19.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Violet chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.39,0:20:27.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Would it pain you{\i0}\N{\i1}to wear some color, Your Grace?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.56,0:20:31.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The London season{\i0}\N{\i1}is already terribly monotonous as it is.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.11,0:20:32.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Must your wardrobe do the same?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.03,0:20:36.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I was told this look is all the rage.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Certainly not mine.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.62,0:20:39.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Take my arm, before you make us late.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.34,0:20:53.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So, you are not dead, after all.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.59,0:20:56.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My lady, we were not expecting your visit.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.13,0:20:58.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Not once seen in London,{\i0}\N{\i1}no news of your education,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.55,0:21:00.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}not a word about you from your father.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.14,0:21:03.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yet here you are, alive and breathing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.64,0:21:06.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Stand up, boy, so I may look at you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.07,0:21:13.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your mother would weep{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.53,0:21:15.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to know her dearest friend{\i0}\N{\i1}was a stranger to her son.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.45,0:21:18.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You look just like her.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.99,0:21:20.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And a good thing too.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.29,0:21:24.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lady Danbury, my lord.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.58,0:21:31.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I see you've not learned any manners.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.30,0:21:33.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Have you learned to read,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.13,0:21:35.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to write,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.63,0:21:37.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to ride a horse, to fence?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.76,0:21:40.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then, why ever are you not in school?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.98,0:21:46.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I c-- c-- can{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.81,0:21:47.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}n-- n-- not{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.23,0:21:50.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}s-- s-- speak.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.99,0:21:59.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}When I was a girl, some centuries ago,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.57,0:22:01.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was afraid even of my own reflection.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.62,0:22:05.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I entered a room and attempted{\i0}\N{\i1}to dissolve into the shadows.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.75,0:22:09.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But there is only so long one{\i0}\N{\i1}in a position such as ours can hide.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.58,0:22:13.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I knew I would have to step{\i0}\N{\i1}into the light someday,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.30,0:22:15.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I could not very well be frightened.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.26,0:22:20.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So, instead, I made myself frightening.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.14,0:22:23.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I sharpened my wit,{\i0}\N{\i1}my wardrobe, and my eye,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.51,0:22:26.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I made myself{\i0}\N{\i1}the most terrifying creature{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.85,0:22:28.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}in any room I entered.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.06,0:22:30.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Come.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:36.40,0:22:39.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You can speak.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.36,0:22:42.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I understood you well enough.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.66,0:22:46.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And I will help you{\i0}\N{\i1}to overcome this stammer of yours.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.95,0:22:50.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But in exchange, you must promise me{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.25,0:22:54.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that when you step into the light…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.21,0:22:59.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you will be worthy{\i0}\N{\i1}of the attention you command.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.63,0:23:01.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hmm?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.77,0:23:09.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[guests talking, laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.58,0:23:28.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A dance, Miss Bridgerton?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.29,0:23:32.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall need someone else{\i0}\N{\i1}to seek me a glass of ratafia, then.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.29,0:23:33.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lord Bridgerton…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.67,0:23:35.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}do me the honor?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.59,0:23:38.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course, Lady Danbury.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.09,0:23:46.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Six balls no more.{\i0}\N{\i1}I must have you at eight.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.81,0:23:48.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Along with a picnic.{\i0}\N{\i1}-A picnic?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.64,0:23:50.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am afraid we are required{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.39,0:23:52.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to fan the flames of our charade.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.27,0:23:55.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, because of Lord Berbrooke, I presume?{\i0}\N{\i1}I heard.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:56.61,0:24:01.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We must make him believe that you are{\i0}\N{\i1}on the very precipice of a proposal…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:01.95,0:24:03.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}so he will leave me alone.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.11,0:24:05.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I should hope{\i0}\N{\i1}I do not lose my balance, then.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:05.41,0:24:06.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I should hope not, either,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.91,0:24:08.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}for you will be glued{\i0}\N{\i1}to my side all evening.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.45,0:24:11.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And we must look like{\i0}\N{\i1}we are enjoying ourselves,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:11.66,0:24:12.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}as difficult as that may be.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:12.87,0:24:14.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes, quite.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:16.50,0:24:18.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[classical dance music playing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:27.76,0:24:29.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[inaudible dialogue]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:07.22,0:25:08.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[music ends]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:09.39,0:25:10.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Go dance with your sister.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:11.06,0:25:12.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Why?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Because I asked you to!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:13.43,0:25:14.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Benedict groans]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:15.73,0:25:17.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Anthony] Perhaps I was unclear.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:17.31,0:25:19.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is it your wish{\i0}\N{\i1}for me to insult your sister, Bridgerton?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:19.65,0:25:20.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}On the contrary.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:20.57,0:25:22.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You wish your sister{\i0}\N{\i1}to marry a loathsome toad, then.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:22.65,0:25:23.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Nigel] Lord Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:24.03,0:25:25.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Forgive the intrusion,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:25.78,0:25:27.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but, if need be,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:27.45,0:25:30.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I will happily restate my intentions{\i0}\N{\i1}with respect to your sister.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:30.45,0:25:34.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She is a prize I have long coveted{\i0}\N{\i1}for her beauty, for her grace--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:34.62,0:25:35.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For her powerful right hook?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:37.00,0:25:39.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I must know whether I can count on you{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:39.21,0:25:41.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to handle this misunderstanding, my lord?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:41.92,0:25:44.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I certainly wish to avoid{\i0}\N{\i1}any kind of embarrassment.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:44.55,0:25:45.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Rather late for that.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:46.68,0:25:49.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you too friendly with the duke{\i0}\N{\i1}or simply intimidated by his rank--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:49.55,0:25:50.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Easy, Berbrooke.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:50.89,0:25:52.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I assured you I will resolve the matter,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:52.89,0:25:55.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}a matter which I shall remind the duke{\i0}\N{\i1}is none of his concern.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:55.77,0:25:57.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps you're not the authority{\i0}\N{\i1}on what concerns me,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:57.85,0:25:59.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}nor on the matter{\i0}\N{\i1}of Lord Berbrooke's character.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:00.94,0:26:03.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall do my best{\i0}\N{\i1}by your sister, Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:03.11,0:26:06.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And perhaps even she might learn{\i0}\N{\i1}to return my affections over time.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:06.40,0:26:07.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do come off it, Berbrooke.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:07.82,0:26:10.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I presume he failed to mention{\i0}\N{\i1}how he got that purple eye.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:11.07,0:26:13.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I was careless with a cabinet door.{\i0}\N{\i1}-He was careless with his honor.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:14.29,0:26:16.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He attempted something last night{\i0}\N{\i1}I shan't dignify with words{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:16.87,0:26:18.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}when your sister planted a facer.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:18.96,0:26:20.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Deservedly so.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:23.25,0:26:24.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My lord, you must know--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:24.71,0:26:26.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne would have told me{\i0}\N{\i1}if this were true.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:28.76,0:26:29.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Would she?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:36.81,0:26:39.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You will never speak{\i0}\N{\i1}to my sister again, Berbrooke.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:39.56,0:26:40.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But we are to be married.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:40.65,0:26:43.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are to be buried{\i0}\N{\i1}if you so much as look in her direction.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:46.32,0:26:49.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Be grateful you will not take a punch{\i0}\N{\i1}from yet another Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:52.45,0:26:54.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What has happened? Brother?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:54.33,0:26:57.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You need not worry about Berbrooke.{\i0}\N{\i1}Sister, it is done.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:58.62,0:26:59.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs deeply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:04.50,0:27:06.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You told him?{\i0}\N{\i1}-I had to say something.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:06.59,0:27:09.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-All will be well, though, I assure you.{\i0}\N{\i1}-You assure me?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:09.97,0:27:11.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Despite what you{\i0}\N{\i1}and my brother may think,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:11.97,0:27:15.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am quite capable of speaking for myself.{\i0}\N{\i1}You had no right.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:15.51,0:27:17.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I was trying to help.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Well, you did not.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:18.14,0:27:21.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}All you did{\i0}\N{\i1}was underestimate Nigel's entitlement.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:21.90,0:27:23.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Not to mention, people are watching.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:24.86,0:27:26.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You cannot assure me of anything.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:38.20,0:27:41.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A crush of an evening, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:42.83,0:27:44.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Would you not agree?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:45.17,0:27:48.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The young lady{\i0}\N{\i1}is as rare a treasure as there is.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:49.01,0:27:51.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do try not to bungle it up.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:52.51,0:27:54.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hmm? Thank you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:54.72,0:27:56.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And how have you been?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:02.02,0:28:04.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I think I shall take the air tonight.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:14.41,0:28:15.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Only me, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:16.28,0:28:17.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you following me, Berbrooke?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:17.99,0:28:19.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I thought this matter settled.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:19.58,0:28:22.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It was settled{\i0}\N{\i1}until you had to go and spoil it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:22.50,0:28:24.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I implore you to speak again{\i0}\N{\i1}with the viscount.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:24.42,0:28:26.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Last night was a mistake, I admit.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:26.46,0:28:27.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A temporary lack of judgment.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:28.04,0:28:29.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You understand that, do you not?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:29.59,0:28:33.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There is not and never will be any kind{\i0}\N{\i1}of understanding between the two of us.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:33.38,0:28:36.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Go home, Berbrooke.{\i0}\N{\i1}-But you do not need her.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:36.43,0:28:37.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You're a duke.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:37.72,0:28:41.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You already have the money,{\i0}\N{\i1}and the connections, and the standing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:41.14,0:28:44.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I {\i0}<span style="style2">need {\i0}{\i1}her.{\i0}\N{\i1}Why can you not just let me have this one?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:44.44,0:28:46.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I think it really ought{\i0}\N{\i1}to be up to Miss Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:46.77,0:28:49.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}When I am buying a horse,{\i0}\N{\i1}I do not negotiate with the horse.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:49.23,0:28:50.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Should you continue to follow me--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:50.78,0:28:52.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why, then, have you not asked for her hand{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:52.57,0:28:55.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}if you are so fond of her,{\i0}\N{\i1}and she so smitten with you?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:55.11,0:28:57.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why have you not already proposed?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:58.07,0:28:59.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Unless you have already had her.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:02.08,0:29:03.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you have, you must tell me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:03.71,0:29:07.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For if I had already known{\i0}\N{\i1}she was loose and damaged, not intact,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:07.54,0:29:09.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I never would have--{\i0}\N{\i1}-Stop talking.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:10.50,0:29:13.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall not have you question{\i0}\N{\i1}the lady's unimpeachable honor again.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:13.34,0:29:14.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:15.59,0:29:18.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes, very well.{\i0}\N{\i1}That is all I had hoped to hear.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:18.64,0:29:21.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You do not deserve to breathe{\i0}\N{\i1}the same air as her.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:21.60,0:29:23.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Now, go home.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:23.52,0:29:24.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And you do?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:25.02,0:29:27.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've heard the stories{\i0}\N{\i1}of your father, Hastings.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:27.44,0:29:31.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know how badly he wanted a son, an heir,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:31.19,0:29:33.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I know how badly he tried to get one{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:33.15,0:29:35.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}when it seemed{\i0}\N{\i1}your poor mother could not deliver.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:35.70,0:29:40.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If anyone were to ever turn a blind eye{\i0}\N{\i1}to a man's temporary lack of judgment,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:40.91,0:29:41.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}it would be you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:41.83,0:29:43.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The apple should not fall very far,{\i0}\N{\i1}should it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:43.83,0:29:45.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[overlapping grunts]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:56.93,0:29:58.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Nigel grunting, moaning]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:05.31,0:30:08.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Grace, may I present Lady Danbury{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:08.19,0:30:10.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and Lord Basset?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:17.49,0:30:18.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:19.28,0:30:21.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}this is a most unwelcome intrusion.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:21.70,0:30:25.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I thought Your Grace might be relieved{\i0}\N{\i1}to know that your son is alive and well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:25.79,0:30:28.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your staff seemed{\i0}\N{\i1}somewhat surprised by the fact.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:28.79,0:30:30.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What is the point of your visit?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:33.34,0:30:36.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am receiving high marks{\i0}\N{\i1}in all of my studies, sir.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:37.88,0:30:39.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I ride, and I fence, and I shoot…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:41.30,0:30:43.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}exceptionally well, I am told.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:46.72,0:30:47.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I even…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:51.15,0:30:52.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:54.19,0:30:56.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are my worst failure.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:57.49,0:30:59.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I beg your pardon?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:59.70,0:31:01.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am sure you do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:01.11,0:31:02.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shan't again.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:03.37,0:31:06.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Might I remind you that this boy{\i0}\N{\i1}is to be the next Duke of Hastings,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:06.29,0:31:09.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and that he requires whatever reserves{\i0}\N{\i1}of fatherly nature reside{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:09.75,0:31:11.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}in that frigid heart of yours?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:11.88,0:31:12.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You may…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:13.54,0:31:15.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}so long as I may remind you of your place,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:16.55,0:31:18.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}which is out of my sight{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:18.46,0:31:20.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and with your bitch mouth shut.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:24.60,0:31:27.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wrote to you many times{\i0}\N{\i1}to let you know I'm…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:28.73,0:31:30.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm not… [hesitates]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:31.56,0:31:32.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}not dead.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:35.23,0:31:36.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did you receive my letters?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:37.03,0:31:39.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is a deep enough wound{\i0}\N{\i1}to live with the knowledge{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:39.11,0:31:41.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that you shall one day inherit Hastings,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:42.03,0:31:45.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but to witness your struggle{\i0}\N{\i1}is too great an insult.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:46.33,0:31:49.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are as useless{\i0}\N{\i1}as your mother proved to be,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:50.37,0:31:53.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}so I shall pursue the same recourse{\i0}\N{\i1}with you as I did with her,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:54.58,0:31:58.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to forget{\i0}\N{\i1}that you ever sullied these halls.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:21.99,0:32:24.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">This author has often thought the heart{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:24.57,0:32:26.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}a most curious of instruments,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:26.66,0:32:28.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}heeding neither reason nor rank.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:28.99,0:32:32.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For what possible explanation{\i0}\N{\i1}might Miss Bridgerton have{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:32.96,0:32:35.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}for entertaining the suit of a mere baron{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:35.58,0:32:38.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}when she seems to have secured a duke?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:38.50,0:32:42.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Could the debutante's mind{\i0}\N{\i1}not be the only thing amiss?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:42.88,0:32:44.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The recipe is my own, miss.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:46.26,0:32:48.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm certain the duke {\i0}\N{\i1}should find it appealing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:48.39,0:32:50.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It does not matter{\i0}\N{\i1}what the duke thinks, Rose.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:50.81,0:32:52.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He is gallant, is he not?{\i0}\N{\i1}With refined taste--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:53.02,0:32:53.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Stop.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:56.56,0:32:57.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is the rouge not to your liking?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:00.86,0:33:01.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:03.15,0:33:04.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is perfect.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:06.11,0:33:07.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I should like some more.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:13.29,0:33:16.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[attendees talking, laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:17.71,0:33:20.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">Let it be known, dear reader,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:20.25,0:33:24.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that if this bizarre behavior portends{\i0}\N{\i1}yet another scandal,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:24.55,0:33:27.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}then be sure that I shall uncover it,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:27.80,0:33:31.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}for there is nothing{\i0}\N{\i1}like an excursion into nature{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:31.31,0:33:34.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to lift the spirits and loosen the tongue.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:35.27,0:33:37.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I hear she may be courting{\i0}\N{\i1}with bumbling Berbrooke.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:37.65,0:33:39.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Quite a good match for her,{\i0}\N{\i1}I rather think.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:39.77,0:33:40.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both snickering]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:46.20,0:33:49.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Mama, might I go play with Eloise?{\i0}\N{\i1}-A lady does not play, Penelope.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:49.66,0:33:52.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Forgive me, Mama. Might I go{\i0}\N{\i1}promenade for suitors with Eloise?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:52.58,0:33:53.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Very well, then.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:57.46,0:34:00.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What have you learned from your maid,{\i0}\N{\i1}the one who is in the family way?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:00.84,0:34:04.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-What happened? How did it happen?{\i0}\N{\i1}-She said it was love.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:05.13,0:34:08.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Love? That doesn't stand to reason.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:08.22,0:34:09.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No, it certainly does not.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:09.84,0:34:11.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Look at my mama. Three children.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:11.93,0:34:14.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Would anyone presume{\i0}\N{\i1}that had anything to do with love?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:14.47,0:34:16.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, what else did she say?{\i0}\N{\i1}Was she not frightened?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:17.06,0:34:18.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}More…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:18.73,0:34:20.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}sad than frightened.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:20.56,0:34:23.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But there may be a chance for her{\i0}\N{\i1}to have a happy ending yet, I suppose.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:23.73,0:34:26.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She wants to escape to the country,{\i0}\N{\i1}where she and her love will marry.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:26.78,0:34:29.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then she has even greater reason{\i0}\N{\i1}to be frightened.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:29.49,0:34:33.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Once she is married, her life is over.{\i0}\N{\i1}Scarcely an escape, Penelope.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:33.24,0:34:34.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, that poor maid!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:48.01,0:34:50.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was not aware, sister,{\i0}\N{\i1}of what Berbrooke attempted.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:50.80,0:34:53.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would have helped you.{\i0}\N{\i1}You should have told me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:53.43,0:34:55.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Would you have believed me?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:55.97,0:34:57.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did you only change your mind{\i0}\N{\i1}about Lord Berbrooke{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:57.98,0:34:59.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}because another man told you the truth?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:59.77,0:35:01.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You truly esteem me so little?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:01.35,0:35:05.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}After I apprised you of my wishes,{\i0}\N{\i1}and you proceeded to ignore them…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:05.15,0:35:06.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}yes, brother, I do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:06.65,0:35:08.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[galloping horse approaches]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:16.37,0:35:18.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You are late.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Apologies.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:18.16,0:35:19.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Should we rejoin your family{\i0}\N{\i1}at their camp?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:20.00,0:35:21.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Certainly not.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:22.13,0:35:25.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We must promenade past the group{\i0}\N{\i1}of men playing their games up ahead.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:30.88,0:35:32.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Whatever happened to your hand?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:32.80,0:35:33.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Boxing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:33.80,0:35:36.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's an absurdity that passes{\i0}\N{\i1}for entertainment amongst men.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:36.85,0:35:40.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-My cuff, button it.{\i0}\N{\i1}-I beg your pardon?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:48.82,0:35:51.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You need not feel your evident worry.{\i0}\N{\i1}Berbrooke is--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:52.07,0:35:54.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Have you not heard{\i0}\N{\i1}what Whistledown writes of me still?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:54.41,0:35:57.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No. Even if you believe{\i0}\N{\i1}Lord Berbrooke is taken care of,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:57.66,0:35:59.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}our ruse is not finished.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:59.08,0:36:00.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm still in need of a husband.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:00.54,0:36:02.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though I am flattered,{\i0}\N{\i1}I'm afraid I must reject your proposal.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:03.00,0:36:05.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes, I know.{\i0}\N{\i1}You are not the marrying type.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:06.42,0:36:09.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yet have you considered{\i0}\N{\i1}you are not the type women wish to marry?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:09.42,0:36:11.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I suppose if I were forced {\i0}\N{\i1}to take a wife,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:11.13,0:36:12.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you would be{\i0}\N{\i1}the least objectionable option.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:12.88,0:36:14.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Is that meant to be a compliment?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Yes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:14.80,0:36:18.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But it is no matter, for you wish{\i0}\N{\i1}to marry for love, do you not?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:19.27,0:36:20.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course I do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:22.98,0:36:23.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They still looking?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:25.23,0:36:26.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[men chuckling]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:27.69,0:36:28.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[man 1] Here he comes now.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:32.61,0:36:33.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Nigel] Bridgerton!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:34.03,0:36:35.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What have you done?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:38.08,0:36:40.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I bring cheerful news, Bridgertons.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:40.62,0:36:42.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have taken matters in my own hands{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:42.37,0:36:45.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and sought a special license{\i0}\N{\i1}for my wedding to Miss Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:45.71,0:36:48.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-There is to be no wedding.{\i0}\N{\i1}-I told you. The arrangement is canceled.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:48.79,0:36:50.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lord Berbrooke,{\i0}\N{\i1}you look in a great deal of pain.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:50.88,0:36:52.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Shall we continue this{\i0}\N{\i1}in a more private location?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:52.97,0:36:55.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I require no further conversation.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:55.13,0:36:58.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though, perhaps I am finally speaking{\i0}\N{\i1}to the true head of the Bridgerton house.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:58.39,0:36:59.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For if it were you,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:59.31,0:37:02.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I imagine you would have instructed{\i0}\N{\i1}your sister to take better care{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:02.68,0:37:04.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}than to encourage certain attentions{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:04.77,0:37:06.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}while alone with me{\i0}\N{\i1}on the Dark Walk at Vauxhall.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:06.81,0:37:11.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course, mere hearsay{\i0}\N{\i1}of such a scandal could wreak havoc{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:11.19,0:37:13.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}on even the most influential of families.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:13.57,0:37:16.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What would someone like,{\i0}\N{\i1}say, Lady Whistledown do{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:17.03,0:37:18.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}with such unseemly information?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:18.82,0:37:20.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Is that a threat?{\i0}\N{\i1}-It is certainly not.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:21.37,0:37:23.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Because in three days, I am to marry.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:25.21,0:37:26.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have the diamond of the season.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:26.75,0:37:29.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have the very best the ton has to offer.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:29.59,0:37:30.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have a Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:31.55,0:37:35.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And I shall save her,{\i0}\N{\i1}as well as your entire family,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:35.22,0:37:38.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}from the ruin{\i0}\N{\i1}which you could not protect them.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:42.39,0:37:43.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:43.47,0:37:46.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I look forward to the union{\i0}\N{\i1}of our great families.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:47.73,0:37:48.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:49.44,0:37:50.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hastings.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:55.36,0:37:57.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Anthony] I must issue{\i0}\N{\i1}my challenge to Berbrooke straight away.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:57.66,0:37:58.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Violet] Anthony…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:58.57,0:38:00.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I assure you{\i0}\N{\i1}I've been properly trained in the manner.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:01.08,0:38:03.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are not to duel with Lord Berbrooke.{\i0}\N{\i1}Do you understand me?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:04.33,0:38:07.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not care what kind of training{\i0}\N{\i1}you think you may have.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:07.21,0:38:09.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is illegal,{\i0}\N{\i1}not to mention positively horrific.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:09.50,0:38:11.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Gentlemen are left{\i0}\N{\i1}with no other choice, Mother.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:11.88,0:38:14.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}When a young woman,{\i0}\N{\i1}let alone one's sister,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:14.13,0:38:17.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}is rumored to be dishonored,{\i0}\N{\i1}the consequences shall be deadly!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:17.17,0:38:18.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is no solution.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:19.18,0:38:22.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Should Lord Berbrooke decide{\i0}\N{\i1}to make good on his threat{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:22.10,0:38:25.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}before you shoot him dead, brother,{\i0}\N{\i1}what happens then?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:26.64,0:38:30.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He may decide{\i0}\N{\i1}to open his tiny mouth at any moment,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:30.40,0:38:32.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and then I shall be ruined…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:33.40,0:38:34.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}as will we all.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:38.11,0:38:39.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I must marry Nigel Berbrooke.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:40.74,0:38:42.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is the only choice.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:59.34,0:39:00.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne sniffles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:00.80,0:39:02.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Rose, can you leave us for a moment?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:05.35,0:39:06.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne sniffles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:18.24,0:39:19.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have taught you to believe{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:19.99,0:39:23.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that marriage is the best{\i0}\N{\i1}that life has to offer,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:24.24,0:39:25.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and that remains true.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:26.62,0:39:30.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But it is not simply a partner{\i0}\N{\i1}that marriage provides.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:31.04,0:39:34.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You will have comfort{\i0}\N{\i1}and a house to tend,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:34.96,0:39:37.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and most importantly, children.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:39.42,0:39:42.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You will throw yourself{\i0}\N{\i1}into raising your family,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:42.43,0:39:44.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and you will find much joy.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:45.93,0:39:47.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am certain.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:52.65,0:39:53.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You and Papa…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:56.65,0:39:58.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The two of you were so beautiful, Mama.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:01.11,0:40:02.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That is what I wanted.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:04.62,0:40:06.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That is all I hoped to one day find.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:08.29,0:40:09.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As did I.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:14.46,0:40:16.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Violet chuckles affectionately]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:25.85,0:40:27.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[exhales]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:28.72,0:40:30.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Benedict] Eloise Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:32.27,0:40:33.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Eloise groans]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:40.19,0:40:41.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Go on, then.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:41.82,0:40:43.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Chastise me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:45.53,0:40:46.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Spare one for me?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:00.25,0:41:02.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Suppose I desire something different.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:03.01,0:41:04.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-How do you mean?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Just different.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:05.76,0:41:08.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I watch Daphne prepare for these balls{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:08.18,0:41:10.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}with all of those dresses{\i0}\N{\i1}and the many suitors,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:10.93,0:41:12.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I am exhausted.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:13.06,0:41:14.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Suppose I want a different life,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:14.69,0:41:18.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that I truly believe{\i0}\N{\i1}I am quite capable of something more,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:19.23,0:41:21.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}even when I am not allowed{\i0}\N{\i1}to have anything else.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:23.94,0:41:26.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then I would say…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:28.28,0:41:29.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that you're not the only one.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:41.17,0:41:42.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[overlapping grunts]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:43.71,0:41:44.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon moans]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:49.93,0:41:51.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Still on that dance floor{\i0}\N{\i1}with Miss Bridgerton?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:54.35,0:41:55.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How is she?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:55.39,0:41:57.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[exhales sharply] She is to marry.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:57.23,0:41:59.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then you are free to do as you please.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:01.07,0:42:01.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Another.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:27.13,0:42:28.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[exhales lightly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:56.08,0:42:57.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Majesty.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:57.16,0:42:58.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[piano sonata playing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:08.38,0:43:09.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sniffs sharply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:12.05,0:43:13.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sniffles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:14.01,0:43:15.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[grunts lightly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:15.60,0:43:16.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What do you think?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:20.39,0:43:21.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of the music?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:23.23,0:43:24.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I find it quite beautiful.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:26.82,0:43:27.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is it Mozart?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:28.90,0:43:32.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I became acquainted with Mr. Mozart{\i0}\N{\i1}when he was not ten years old.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:32.16,0:43:36.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The boy accompanied me as I sang an aria,{\i0}\N{\i1}and I declared then and there{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:36.12,0:43:38.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that he should become{\i0}\N{\i1}one of the finest composers in Europe.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:38.91,0:43:41.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And certainly you were right.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:41.75,0:43:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm rarely wrong about such matters.{\i0}\N{\i1}Do you know why?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:45.29,0:43:47.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Because when I choose{\i0}\N{\i1}to extend to someone my favor,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:48.01,0:43:49.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I expect them to make good on it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:49.72,0:43:51.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Your Majesty, is this about--{\i0}\N{\i1}-Brimsley!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:52.51,0:43:53.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fresh snuff.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:00.77,0:44:03.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-That one is a terrible gossip.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[door closes]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:03.35,0:44:05.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If we were to speak freely{\i0}\N{\i1}in his presence,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:05.11,0:44:08.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}before long, the whole of England{\i0}\N{\i1}would know our business.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:09.32,0:44:10.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I see.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:12.11,0:44:13.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I suppose you do see.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:14.32,0:44:15.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I expected a great future{\i0}\N{\i1}for your daughter{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:16.08,0:44:18.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}upon her entrance into society.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:18.24,0:44:21.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A future with someone like a duke,{\i0}\N{\i1}perhaps.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:21.83,0:44:23.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A pairing like that…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:24.71,0:44:25.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:26.67,0:44:29.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}it would certainly be{\i0}\N{\i1}most enchanting indeed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:29.96,0:44:31.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Queen Charlotte clears throat]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:35.09,0:44:36.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[door closes]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:43.31,0:44:44.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As I was saying,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:44.73,0:44:47.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the glow of success{\i0}\N{\i1}benefited not only the young maestro.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:48.69,0:44:51.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Surely the entire Mozart family{\i0}\N{\i1}would have felt the repercussions,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:51.90,0:44:54.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}had their boys stayed forever in Salzburg.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:58.24,0:44:59.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Would you not agree?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:06.83,0:45:09.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why, yes. Yes, I would.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:11.05,0:45:12.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But what are we to do, ma'am?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:12.72,0:45:16.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We are to invite Lady Berbrooke{\i0}\N{\i1}over for tea, Mrs. Wilson, at once.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:23.10,0:45:26.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Nigel is my one and only child.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Violet] Mm-hmm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:26.48,0:45:28.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Very special boy, indeed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:28.23,0:45:32.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}In fact, I often say{\i0}\N{\i1}God did not bless me with another{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:32.40,0:45:35.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}because perfection{\i0}\N{\i1}had already been achieved. [chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:35.61,0:45:36.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My goodness.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:36.66,0:45:37.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Berbrooke] Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:37.74,0:45:40.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Not every lady can be so blessed, I know.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:40.83,0:45:42.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Daphne sniffles]{\i0}\N{\i1}-Miss Bridgerton…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:42.83,0:45:45.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}allow me to set my eyes upon you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:47.17,0:45:48.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:48.54,0:45:49.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Certainly healthy.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:50.84,0:45:53.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Even if your countenance is a bit drawn.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:53.34,0:45:54.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne inhales sharply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:54.51,0:45:57.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-It was a terribly late evening.{\i0}\N{\i1}-All the excitement, I suppose.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:57.47,0:45:59.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yet you must try harder, dear.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:59.97,0:46:01.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My Nigel is quite discerning.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:01.85,0:46:05.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He already turned away{\i0}\N{\i1}many more handsome debutantes, saying,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:05.52,0:46:06.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}"Mother…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:06.73,0:46:10.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles] {\i0}\N{\i1}…I prize accomplishment over beauty."{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:11.44,0:46:12.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Can you believe it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:15.40,0:46:16.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[crunching loudly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:17.45,0:46:19.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[bell rings]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Wilson] Ooh! Oh!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:20.28,0:46:23.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That mistress of yours is going{\i0}\N{\i1}through the biscuits quick.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:23.66,0:46:26.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do not worry, Rose. I shall handle it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:29.71,0:46:30.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Housekeepers…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:31.42,0:46:33.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They believe themselves{\i0}\N{\i1}the sun and the moon,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:33.21,0:46:35.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}when in truth, it is us lady's maids{\i0}\N{\i1}that do all the hard work.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:35.84,0:46:37.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Celia chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:37.09,0:46:38.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have one just like her.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:38.93,0:46:40.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are quite fortunate, though.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:40.39,0:46:41.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How troublesome could a household be{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:41.93,0:46:44.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}with only Lady Berbrooke{\i0}\N{\i1}and young Lord Berbrooke to look after?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:45.02,0:46:47.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, you have no idea.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:48.94,0:46:53.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You ate but not one bite at tea, my dear!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:53.52,0:46:56.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A young lady must be well fed{\i0}\N{\i1}if she is to bear children.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:56.78,0:47:00.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Kippers on rye every morning{\i0}\N{\i1}worked wonders for me{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:00.11,0:47:01.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}when I conceived my Nigel.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:01.99,0:47:04.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Berbrooke and Violet chuckling]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:07.08,0:47:08.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasps] What have you found?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:08.71,0:47:09.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne] What is going on?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:09.92,0:47:11.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You could not think{\i0}\N{\i1}I'd ask that woman for tea{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:11.79,0:47:13.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}without a thought for you, could you?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:13.34,0:47:16.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The help hears everything, as we all know.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:16.38,0:47:17.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She has heard a good deal, in fact.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:17.88,0:47:20.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lord Berbrooke has a boy{\i0}\N{\i1}by one of his maids{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:20.68,0:47:22.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that he refused to provide for.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:22.39,0:47:24.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sent the maid and child away{\i0}\N{\i1}to live off scraps.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:24.60,0:47:25.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Horrible man.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:25.51,0:47:28.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Horrible enough{\i0}\N{\i1}for us to be rid of him, let us pray.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:29.77,0:47:31.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, he-- He will only deny it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:32.65,0:47:35.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And who will believe a group of women{\i0}\N{\i1}over a man's word?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:35.90,0:47:36.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps no one.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:37.73,0:47:42.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But they will if Lady Whistledown does.{\i0}\N{\i1}So we shall do what women do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:43.24,0:47:44.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We shall talk.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:48.25,0:47:50.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And the only reason he married her{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:50.33,0:47:54.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}is because his {\i0}<span style="style2">père{\i0}{\i1} squandered{\i0}\N{\i1}the accounts on some scheme in America.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:54.50,0:47:56.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasps theatrically] Oh, {\i0}<span style="style2">mon Dieu.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:56.80,0:47:59.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is it not the most lurid story{\i0}\N{\i1}of the season?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:00.92,0:48:02.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps not the most lurid.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:05.18,0:48:07.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, every baron has a bastard.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:07.64,0:48:10.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A bastard he sent away{\i0}\N{\i1}before the miss even popped?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:11.64,0:48:14.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You don't say.{\i0}\N{\i1}Well, we must tell Jennie and Mary.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:18.15,0:48:20.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[inaudible dialogue]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:21.65,0:48:24.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">It has come to this author's attention{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:24.74,0:48:28.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that the ton is abuzz{\i0}\N{\i1}with a most sordid tale.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:33.71,0:48:38.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is said{\i0}\N{\i1}one cannot judge a book by its cover.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:38.21,0:48:41.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But in the case{\i0}\N{\i1}of the bumbling Baron Berbrooke,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:41.34,0:48:46.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}it seems his displeasing appearance{\i0}\N{\i1}is quite an apt metaphor{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:46.51,0:48:49.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}for the state of affairs in his household.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:50.77,0:48:52.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would not be surprised{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:52.35,0:48:56.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}if Lord Berbrooke were called away{\i0}\N{\i1}to the country on alleged business…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:56.94,0:48:58.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Business which, perhaps,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:58.90,0:49:02.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}might involve sending{\i0}\N{\i1}some much overdue funds{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:02.49,0:49:05.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to one former maid and young boy,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:05.61,0:49:08.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}who we can only hope{\i0}\N{\i1}takes after his mother.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:11.50,0:49:14.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have heard talk{\i0}\N{\i1}that Berbrooke has left town.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:15.54,0:49:18.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I think this solution to our problem{\i0}\N{\i1}did not come about by chance.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:25.22,0:49:27.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am resolved to handle matters{\i0}\N{\i1}differently in the future.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:29.93,0:49:31.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Or perhaps not at all.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:34.14,0:49:37.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know society has dictated{\i0}\N{\i1}your present role in this family, Anthony,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:37.60,0:49:41.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but with Daphne officially out,{\i0}\N{\i1}I assure you, I am more than capable.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:45.86,0:49:46.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is for Daphne.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:48.20,0:49:49.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Tulips.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:50.33,0:49:51.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They symbolize passion.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:53.08,0:49:56.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A most appropriate hem for your sister{\i0}\N{\i1}when she decides to marry the duke.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:58.54,0:50:00.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps your bride would like the same.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:02.96,0:50:04.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Good night, Mother.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:07.30,0:50:09.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Violet chuckles lightly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:20.81,0:50:21.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[door opens]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:26.74,0:50:30.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Surely your mistress does not plan{\i0}\N{\i1}on confining me to this bedroom forever.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:30.74,0:50:31.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Varney chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:31.70,0:50:35.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I should think one has only herself{\i0}\N{\i1}to blame for her confinement, miss.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:48.55,0:50:49.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[footsteps approaching]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:59.14,0:51:00.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Eloise.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:01.81,0:51:03.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Uh… Did you need something?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:05.19,0:51:06.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:09.03,0:51:09.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:10.61,0:51:12.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am… [clears throat]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:12.57,0:51:15.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}…glad this business{\i0}\N{\i1}with Nigel Berbrooke is over for you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:16.87,0:51:17.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Thank you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:21.79,0:51:25.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You hear stories{\i0}\N{\i1}about appalling arrangements,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:25.59,0:51:28.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and hopeless endings, and…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:29.67,0:51:31.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, it is all very frightening.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:32.43,0:51:35.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Eloise, you mustn't worry about--{\i0}\N{\i1}-Are you not frightened, too, sister?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:36.97,0:51:39.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of marriage? Of… children?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:40.69,0:51:42.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I find children to be delightful.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:43.86,0:51:46.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though,{\i0}\N{\i1}you are not currently proving my point.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:48.82,0:51:51.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Surely you've not forgotten{\i0}\N{\i1}what happened to Mama?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:52.03,0:51:53.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Her screams that night.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:55.20,0:51:57.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You tried to hide it by singing to me,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:57.49,0:51:58.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but her voice…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:59.58,0:52:00.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}it rattled the windows.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:02.25,0:52:06.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I hear them sometimes still {\i0}\N{\i1}in my dreams.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:08.21,0:52:09.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She almost died…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:10.80,0:52:12.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}mere months after Papa.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:14.18,0:52:15.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Eloise sighs tremulously] {\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:15.76,0:52:17.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course I have not forgotten.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:21.43,0:52:22.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:23.60,0:52:24.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am frightened.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:25.73,0:52:29.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I dare say I would be a fool at this point{\i0}\N{\i1}not to be terrified.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:30.24,0:52:33.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You remember correctly{\i0}\N{\i1}that Mama had a…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:34.53,0:52:35.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}perilous night.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:36.87,0:52:39.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But at dawn, the world had Hyacinth,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:40.20,0:52:42.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and we are all the richer for it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:43.83,0:52:45.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes, Eloise, there…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:45.92,0:52:49.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}are perhaps darker turns in these woods{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:49.63,0:52:51.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}than we've been taught to expect.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:52.97,0:52:55.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There is light to be found at their end.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:56.34,0:52:57.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And I know…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:58.26,0:52:59.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}one day…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:00.27,0:53:01.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}we both will find it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:04.73,0:53:06.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It must be taxing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:07.73,0:53:08.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:10.28,0:53:13.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The game of pretend{\i0}\N{\i1}that you feel you must endlessly maintain.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:18.45,0:53:21.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[rendition of "In My Blood"{\i0}\N{\i1}by Vitamin String Quartet playing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:22.45,0:53:23.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[guests laughing, talking]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:53.74,0:53:55.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Good evening.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:58.03,0:54:01.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You should not have lost your temper{\i0}\N{\i1}with Lord Berbrooke.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:01.41,0:54:03.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You should know something about me,{\i0}\N{\i1}Miss Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:03.91,0:54:05.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I will not tolerate a bully.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:06.12,0:54:08.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And you should know{\i0}\N{\i1}something about me, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:09.33,0:54:10.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I will not have this go wrong.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:11.42,0:54:12.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You mean our ruse?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:14.76,0:54:16.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is more than a ruse now.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:17.47,0:54:19.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is more than a negotiation.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:20.55,0:54:22.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is not just about finding {\i0}\N{\i1}the best match{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:22.76,0:54:24.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to impress Lady Whistledown…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:25.73,0:54:28.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}or the queen, or any member of the ton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:28.52,0:54:32.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is about a life, Your Grace. My life.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:33.32,0:54:35.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I must finally take charge of it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:36.36,0:54:38.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I cannot afford to do otherwise.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:39.03,0:54:40.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So I shall not have this go wrong.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:41.07,0:54:43.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you are not in agreement,{\i0}\N{\i1}then you should tell me now.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:45.75,0:54:46.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall agree…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:47.87,0:54:48.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}on one condition.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:49.04,0:54:51.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You do not understand, Your Grace--{\i0}\N{\i1}-That you call me Simon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:53.38,0:54:57.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If we are truly to seem to be courting,{\i0}\N{\i1}if this is to be a match like no other,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:57.47,0:54:59.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you should call me by my name.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:59.13,0:55:00.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Very well…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:01.89,0:55:02.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Simon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:03.35,0:55:04.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[stifled chuckle]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:04.35,0:55:06.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is there something funny about my name?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:07.56,0:55:09.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No, no, no.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:10.19,0:55:12.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is a perfectly fine name.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:12.56,0:55:13.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, perfectly fine?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:13.98,0:55:16.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Very well… Daphne.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:28.96,0:55:30.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wish to find a husband…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:32.17,0:55:35.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}so that I may have a family, children.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:36.42,0:55:38.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then let us find you a husband.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:56.61,0:55:58.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}May I have the pleasure?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:01.86,0:56:03.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:11.92,0:56:15.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The two of you certainly make{\i0}\N{\i1}a captivating match, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:21.97,0:56:23.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Whatever is bothering you?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:29.81,0:56:32.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}N-Nothing at all, Lady Danbury.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:37.27,0:56:38.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[strained gasping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:47.53,0:56:49.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasping for air]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:49.16,0:56:50.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My… My son.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:51.04,0:56:54.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[strained whispering] You have returned{\i0}\N{\i1}to take your rightful place.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:55.04,0:56:57.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[coughs, gasping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:58.34,0:56:59.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My heart may be failing,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:00.67,0:57:02.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I assure you,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:03.17,0:57:04.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}it swells with pride,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:05.18,0:57:07.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}knowing the duke you have grown into…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:08.64,0:57:09.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[coughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:09.76,0:57:14.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}…and the great Hastings name{\i0}\N{\i1}shall continue.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:14.60,0:57:16.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[labored panting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:16.44,0:57:18.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Listen to me very closely…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:20.61,0:57:23.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}for I have only returned{\i0}\N{\i1}to do but one thing…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:23.19,0:57:24.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[intense music plays]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:24.45,0:57:25.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}…to make you a vow…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:26.57,0:57:28.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the only vow I will ever make in my life.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:31.74,0:57:33.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I will never marry.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:34.33,0:57:36.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I will never sire an heir.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:36.58,0:57:37.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Duke of Hastings gasping wetly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:38.04,0:57:41.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Hastings line will die with me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:41.38,0:57:42.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[strained choking]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:45.05,0:57:47.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are my words clear enough for you, Father?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:50.26,0:57:52.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Speak, you fucking monster.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:52.93,0:57:54.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[tense music intensifies]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:56.27,0:57:58.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Duke of Hastings coughs]{\i0}\N{\i1}-Speak!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:58.27,0:57:59.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sharp breaths]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:58:10.95,0:58:12.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[tense music crescendos]{\i0}
